invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_mont64_mul
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_mul's array is one word short, so at the largest
  word count the word above the running sum, where a round keeps its
  multiple of the modulus, is past the array, and every round reads and
  writes there. A smaller modulus never shows it. rsa_mont64_mul runs the
  function at that count, where each access is a property.

--- old
    // word above them holds u, the round's multiple of m.
    uint64_t t[RSA_MONT64_WORDS_MAX + 2];
--- new
    // word above them holds u, the round's multiple of m.
    uint64_t t[RSA_MONT64_WORDS_MAX + 1];
